Give write_rc a do- sibling.

ORFS fits the per-layer RC that every pre-route timing stage runs on by
regressing routed segment parasitics against extracted ones -- the
procedure in docs/tutorials/SetRC.md, driven by the write_rc and
correlate_rc make targets in flow/util/utils.mk.

write_rc has no do- sibling. flow/Makefile's own comment states the
convention -- "a do- sibling rule that copies the file unconditionally"
-- and do-synth-report, do-klayout, do-step and do-copy all follow it:
the file target decides *whether* to run and delegates with
$(UNSET_AND_MAKE), and the do- target is the single place the invocation
lives. Only write_rc conflates the two, so a caller that does its own
dependency checking -- bazel, through //:rc.bzl -- cannot ask for the
operation.

The file target delegates rather than keeping a second copy of the
$(RUN_CMD) line, which is the same DRY shape as every other do- pair.
That is not a change to make's dependency checking, which is left
exactly as it is for whoever wants to own it.

The bazel side of the same calibration -- staging flow/util's *.tcl and
exporting the four scripts as labels -- is not a patch: ORFS a71b115b9b
deleted flow/util/BUILD, and bazel-orfs now generates it in
orfs_source.bzl's _GENERATE_FLOW_BUILD, which carries both.

Not upstreamed. Retire at the //:bump onto an ORFS that carries a
do-write_rc target.

diff --git a/flow/util/utils.mk b/flow/util/utils.mk
--- a/flow/util/utils.mk
+++ b/flow/util/utils.mk
@@ -113,6 +113,14 @@
 # A pattern rule to write both files with a single run, as the grouped target
 # syntax requires GNU Make 4.3.
 %_nets_rc.csv %_segments_rc.csv:
+	$(UNSET_AND_MAKE) do-write_rc
+
+# The do- sibling, following do-synth-report and the do-step/do-copy
+# families: the file target above decides *whether* to run and delegates
+# here, and this rule is the only place the invocation lives. A caller
+# doing its own dependency checking asks for this one directly.
+.PHONY: do-write_rc
+do-write_rc:
 	$(RUN_CMD) --log $(LOG_DIR)/6_write_rc.log --tee -- $(OPENROAD_CMD) $(UTILS_DIR)/write_rc.tcl
 
 .PHONY: correlate_rc
